            <ArticleTitle>Brachial plexus injuries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>130-2, 134-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There can be few more distressing situations than when a young man sustains a total and irreversible paralysis in his dominant arm. Not only is he left with a useless and anaesthetic limb, but in a high proportion of cases suffers intractable pain. This article will discuss the diagnosis and management of such injuries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
